    "result_text": "There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are a base class and a helper. The full suite ran and is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit logging requirement in the owner create endpoint.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) \u2014 matching the logger name the acceptance test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n2. In `addOwner(...)`, immediately after the successful `saveOwner(owner)` call (so the owner id has been assigned), emit an audit line carrying the three required fields:\n\n```java\nthis.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\nAUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n```\n\nThe log is emitted only on successful create (after all validation/rejection checks and the persist), and the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` are all populated at that point.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The observed audit line during the run confirms the format: `INFO AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`.",
